        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T17:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So in normal onCreateBackendTexture we will fail the call (i.e. return empty BeTex) if the client requests a format we don\u0027t support. The way this is setup right now I think if the AHB claims to know a Vulkan format we will just use that. Then we will end up failing when that BeTex is wrapped into an SkImage/Surface. I wonder if we should be checking our caps to see if we support the given format.\n\nIf we don\u0027t support the format, then I don\u0027t think we have to fail like the normal case. Instead I think we can fall back to importing it as external. We then also have to incorporate this into the isRenderable check above. I.e. we can\u0027t make a renderable thing that has an external format (there actually may be an extension now that allows it but we haven\u0027t add support).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 407,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 407,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "abd83bdc33595977c9fb88302e4e0efee5de2d64",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
