      "lineNbr": 476,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T23:31:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good callout. The spec (https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/html/vkspec.html#_description_123) says that the main differences between `VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL` and `VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_FOREIGN_EXT` are:\n\n1) Foreign queues don\u0027t require the same physical device and driver version as the current `VkInstance`, unlike external\n\n2) All external memory resources support external, but not all of them support foreign. Foreign is more restrictive\n\n3) Transitions to/from foreign queues are more expensive than those to/from external queues\n\nGiven that the client sets up the `VkInstance`, I would imagine that foreign doesn\u0027t really offer that much benefit for us over external. But I suppose there will be cases where the AHwBuffer will be from an \"foreign\" device (relevant TODO: https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/AHardwareBufferVk.cpp#346), in which case foreign would be preferable. \n\nChanged to foreign, but LMKWYT - it sounds like it would be best to make an intelligent decision b/w foreign and external if we know whether the buffer is from a foreign device or not to avoid the costlier transitions to/from foreign queues (though I\u0027m not sure off the top of my head whether we will even realistically encounter a need to transition to/from that queue type often).",
      "parentUuid": "499074e2_051d4682",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 476,
        "startChar": 83,
        "endLine": 476,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "abd83bdc33595977c9fb88302e4e0efee5de2d64",
